Silver Layer Transformation Documentation
Project Overview

The Silver Layer was created to clean, standardize, enrich, and validate raw e-commerce data coming from the Bronze Layer.
This layer prepares the data for analytics, reporting, dashboarding, and future Gold Layer modeling.

The main objectives of the Silver Layer are:

Improve data quality
Remove inconsistencies
Standardize formats
Create business-ready columns
Preserve analytical value
Handle missing and duplicate records properly
1. Customer Table
Table Name

silver.olist_customers

Source

bronze.olist_customers

Transformations Performed
Data Cleaning
Removed unnecessary leading and trailing spaces from customer-related fields.
Standardized customer state values into uppercase format.
Data Validation
Removed records with missing customer IDs because customer_id is the primary business identifier.
Business Purpose

This table is used for:

Customer segmentation
Regional customer analysis
Order-to-customer relationship mapping
Geographic reporting
